# Network model

This branch describes a pipe network. A `Net` collects the `Nodes`, the `Tanks`, the `Pipes`, the `Pumps` and the `Valves`; `network` validates it with a `Liquid` and compiles an immutable `Network` that every analysis takes.

## Choosing A Surface

Write every quantity in SI units. Give every array its node, pipe, pump, valve or tank axis last, and add leading axes to describe a batch of scenarios. Every connected part of the network needs a reservoir or a tank.

## Practical Examples

The examples exercise the principal surface of this branch.

